1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,437
Professor, what would happen

2
00:00:01,457 --> 00:00:02,626
if the Moon suddenly vanished?

3
00:00:03,017 --> 00:00:04,807
You'd notice on the very first night.

4
00:00:04,827 --> 00:00:06,314
The sky would be much darker.

5
00:00:06,695 --> 00:00:07,856
Is that all?

6
00:00:08,244 --> 00:00:08,716
No.

7
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:10,550
The Moon makes most of the tides.

8
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:11,937
Without it, tides would

9
00:00:11,957 --> 00:00:13,120
shrink to a third.

10
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,972
Even corals time their

11
00:00:14,992 --> 00:00:16,643
spawning by moonlight.

12
00:00:16,663 --> 00:00:18,614
Their calendar would break.

13
00:00:18,994 --> 00:00:20,155
What about the Earth?

14
00:00:20,548 --> 00:00:22,108
That's the real danger.

15
00:00:22,128 --> 00:00:24,301
The Moon keeps Earth's axis steady.

16
00:00:24,321 --> 00:00:26,034
Without it, the axis could

17
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:28,022
wobble much more over time, and

18
00:00:28,042 --> 00:00:29,929
the seasons would go haywire.

19
00:00:30,309 --> 00:00:31,795
So the Moon is our balance?

20
00:00:32,185 --> 00:00:32,776
Exactly.

21
00:00:32,796 --> 00:00:34,380
And the Moon moves 3.8 centimeters

22
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,622
away from us every year.

23
00:00:36,002 --> 00:00:37,249
You pick the next question!

24
00:00:37,269 --> 00:00:38,463
Write it in the comments.
